      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 899811820591855403, guid: 0b62242a110afa34499a4d135aa6d7e5, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_Text
      value: "That\u2019s Correct!\n\nRotating the bracelet does not create a new
        arrangement.\nFlipping the bracelet also does not create a new arrangement.\n\nWith
        A fixed, the two circular arrangements are:\n\nABC\n\nACB\n\nHowever, when
        the bracelet is flipped:\n\nABC becomes ACB\n\nACB becomes ABC\n\nSo they
        represent the same arrangement.\n\nThis is why for a bracelet, we divide
        by 2.\n\nBracelet Permutations = \\frac{(n - 1)!}{2}\n\nFor three beads:\n\n\\frac{(3
        - 1)!}{2} = \\frac{2!}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1\n\nThere is only one distinct
        bracelet arrangement."
      objectReference: {fileID: 0}
    - target: {fileID: 938643776309687553, guid: 0b62242a110afa34499a4d135aa6d7e5, type: 3}
      propertyPath: m_fontSize
